40 percent of the schools population consists of 240 boys. Suppose of the schools population comprises N people. Then 40 percent of N equals 240, so 0.4 * N equals 240. Divide both sides with 0.4, we get N = 240/0.4 = 600. Therefore, the schools population is 600 people. If 240 boys compose 40 percent of the school population, then the remaining 60 percent of the students must be girls. The number of girls is 60% of the total population, which is 60% of 600. So, the number of girls is 0.6 * 600 = 360.

So there are 360 girls in the school.

\boxed{360}

